  "answer": "### Short Answer\nThe deadline for filing an estate tax return is within one year from the decedent's death. An extension of up to 30 days may be granted by the Commissioner in meritorious cases.\n\n### Controlling Authorities\nThe relevant provisions are found in Section 89 of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC), which states that the estate tax return must be filed within one year from the decedent's death and allows for a possible extension of up to 30 days.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nThis means that executors or heirs must ensure that the estate tax return is filed within the stipulated one-year period to avoid penalties. If circumstances warrant, they can request an extension, but this must be done within the original deadline and justified to the Commissioner.",
